WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.933
Integrating OT monitoring with a security operations center combines established alert workflows with industrial visibility.

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:21.155
The SOC can provide continuous triage, correlation, case management, and escalation, while OT specialists provide the asset, protocol, process, and safety context needed for sound decisions.

00:00:21.155 --> 00:00:28.607
Forward selected OT events to the SIEM rather than every available record without purpose.

00:00:28.607 --> 00:00:38.464
Preserve useful fields such as asset identity, zone, function, protocol, command category, user, remote session, maintenance state, and criticality.

00:00:38.464 --> 00:00:43.512
Time synchronization and consistent naming are essential for correlation.

00:00:43.512 --> 00:00:48.080
Detection content should link enterprise and OT pathways.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:56.974
A compromised identity, VPN session, jump-host event, firewall connection, and unusual controller communication may form one investigation.

00:00:56.974 --> 00:01:06.831
The SOC needs contacts and runbooks that explain who can validate each stage and which actions require operational approval.

00:01:06.831 --> 00:01:15.725
Monitoring can update asset inventory by revealing new devices, changed communication, or dormant systems returning to service.

00:01:15.725 --> 00:01:22.216
Vulnerability management can use observed reachability and software clues to improve prioritization.

00:01:22.216 --> 00:01:28.707
Architecture teams can compare actual traffic with approved conduits and segmentation policy.

00:01:28.707 --> 00:01:37.121
Governance should define data ownership, retention, access, alert service levels, escalation, monitoring health, and coverage gaps.

00:01:37.121 --> 00:01:48.420
Reports should communicate meaningful risk: unsupported sensors, unmonitored sites, repeated unauthorized access, baseline drift, unresolved high-consequence alerts, and time to coordinated response.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:56.353
Integration does not mean removing OT authority or treating industrial alerts exactly like office endpoints.

00:01:56.353 --> 00:01:59.959
It creates a shared operating model.

00:01:59.959 --> 00:02:07.892
Security operations contribute scale and consistency; engineering and operations contribute process knowledge and safe response.

00:02:07.892 --> 00:02:15.825
Together they turn telemetry into decisions that protect both the network and the physical mission.
